{
 "description": "Push inbox (docs/message-sync.md#push-inbox): what the iPhone notification extension saves from its relay fetch and what the app takes into the message store. `origin`: relay URLs and the store origin they map to (null: refused). `matcher`: events against `matcher_policies` for `matcher_account` (`match`: kept as a pushed message; `keep_as_profile`: kept only as a profile from the presentation refresh). `file`: inbox files the app reads as `file_account` on `file_relay_url` (`accept`: its events are taken; `delete`: a refused file is removed; `ids`: the events kept). `caps`: per-token pruning (files named `<unixms>-<uuid>.json`; `kept`: names left, sorted). `cursor`: the fetch window (`since`) and the cursor after a fetch (`next`). `drain`: pushed rows against the store's kept list, left marks and `room_forgot` stamps (unix seconds); `written`: ids stored. Read by KuzzPushKit tests (Swift) and mobile tests (Dart).",
